<title>BRAZIL: Brazil cenbank sets weaker trade level for real.</title>
<headline>Brazil cenbank sets weaker trade level for real.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank signaled a new weaker trading level for the real currency by buying dollars at 1.018 real and selling dollars at 1.023 real in a buy/sell tender in the commercial foreign exchange market, dealers said.</p>
<p>Under the previous mini-band set on Thursday, the real was traded between 1.017 and 1.022 per dollar.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo Newsroom 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
